# Git and local tooling
.git
.gitignore
**/.nx/cache
# Rewritten by every nx invocation (~19MB). CI runs codegen before `docker build`,
# so without this it lands in the manifests stage's `COPY . .` layer and gets
# re-exported to the layer cache on every build. Bloat only — it cannot bust the
# npm ci layer, which is keyed on the extracted package.json set.
**/.nx/workspace-data
**/.cache

# Rebuilt inside the image
**/node_modules
**/dist

# Dev artifacts
**/coverage
**/*.log
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Not needed for app image builds
docs/
packages/e2e/playwright-report/
output.json
output-worker-graph.json

# Deploy/runtime plumbing. The image build reads nothing from ops/ — only the
# `manifests` stage's wholesale `COPY . .` would otherwise pull it in, and ops/
# holds no package.json, so excluding it changes nothing the build consumes.
ops/

# Compose/Makefile are not part of the build context payload. The compose files
# live at the repo root now (docker-compose-dev.yml / -ci.yml / -prod.yml), so
# they sit directly in the build context — without this glob every compose edit
# would invalidate the context and force a full arm64 rebuild.
docker-compose-*.yml
Makefile
